  "includedPullRequests": [
    {
      "repository": "gordolio/Trio",
      "number": 1712,
      "title": "Read the reservoir from the pump manager instead of storing it",
      "body": "After removing a pump, or deactivating a Medtrum patch or Omnipod pod, Trio kept showing and uploading the old reservoir from monitor/reservoir.json until the new pump reported one.\n\nThe reservoir is not stored anymore. Home and the Nightscout upload read it from the active pump manager's state, so no pump, patch or pod means no reservoir. For Medtrum patchSessionEnded is checked, since MedtrumKit keeps the old value until a new patch is activated (jbr7rr/MedtrumKit#139). For Dana the value is used only after pumpTime is set, since reservoirLevel is 0 until the first sync. The old file is removed at startup, and the unused reservoir input to determine basal and the reservoir check in APSManager are removed.\n",
      "labels": [],
      "url": "https://github.com/nightscout/Trio/pull/1712",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-02T22:15:26Z"
    },
    {
      "repository": "nightscout/Trio",
